-LiteralPath '\\\\\\\"'C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\generated_images\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\01a04df8-1485-7193-be24-139872705880' -Filter '*.png' -File; if (\\\\\\\"'$src.Count -ne 1) { throw \\\\\\\"Expected 1 PNG, found $($src.Count)\\\\\\\" }; Copy-Item -LiteralPath $src[0].FullName -Destination '\\\\\\\"'C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Temp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\story-os-image-o928dxj3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\out.png' -Force; Test-Path -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Temp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\story-os-image-o928dxj3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\out.png'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"execution error: Io(Custom { kind: Other, error: \\\\\\\"windows sandbox: CreateProcessWithLogonW failed: 1385\\\\\\\" })\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":-1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"failed\\\"}}\\r\\nepisodes/10_山难伪纪录片/01_鳌太线_热汤/media/review\\\\manual-production-04-face-check.jsonl:148:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_9\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.cache\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\native\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pwsh.exe\\\\\\\" -Command 'rg -n \\\\\\\"''^\\\\\\\" START_HERE.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"1:# Dali Cat Story OS — START HERE V2.0.3.4\\\\n2:\\\\n3:> 30 秒执行入口。这里不是第二套创作规范，只负责告诉 Agent **先读什么、现在在哪、下一步做什么**。\\\\n4:>\\\\n5:> 创作规则唯一权威：`standards/制作规范_正式版.md`  \\\\n6:> 阶段状态唯一事实源：`<episode>/meta/episode-state.json`\\\\n7:\\\\n8:## 0. 黄金路径（Golden Path）\\\\n9:\\\\n10:```text\\\\n11:恢复上下文\\\\n12:→ 选题 / 去同质化\\\\n13:→ 锁故事与专业分镜\\\\n14:→ 建真实性卡与连续性锚点\\\\n15:→ 三张真实性校准 + 四张视觉准入\\\\n16:→ Visual Lock\\\\n17:→ 批量生产\\\\n18:→ 逐帧审核 / 必要返修\\\\n19:→ Final Checklist\\\\n20:→ 发布\\\\n21:→ 6h / 24h / 48h / 7d 数据回填\\\\n22:```\\\\n23:\\\\n24:机器状态仍只使用仓库原生七阶段：\\\\n25:\\\\n26:```text\\\\n27:IDEA_LOCKED\\\\n28:→ STORYBOARD_LOCKED\\\\n29:→ VISUAL_CALIBRATED\\\\n30:→ PRODUCTION_PASSED\\\\n31:→ PUBLISH_READY\\\\n32:→ PUBLISHED\\\\n33:→ DATA_REVIEWED\\\\n34:```\\\\n35:\\\\n36:**不要新建第二套 stage / status / workflow 状态。**\\\\n37:\\\\n38:## 1. 每次任务只按这个顺序读\\\\n39:\\\\n40:1. 本文件 `START_HERE.md`\\\\n41:2. 根目录 `SKILL.md`\\\\n42:3. 根目录 `AGENTS.md`\\\\n43:4. `standards/制作规范_正式版.md`\\\\n44:5. `standards/AUTHORITY_INDEX.json` 中与当前任务匹配的 active 从属细则\\\\n45:6. 目标剧集 README / docs / 锁定分镜\\\\n46:7. 目标剧集 `meta/episode-state.json`\\\\n47:8. 若 strict=true，再读 `story-gates.json / production-ledger.json / frame-reviews/`\\\\n48:\\\\n49:不要为了“更保险”把整个 `standards/` 全部读一遍。旧版本和 superseded 文件只用于历史追溯。\\\\n50:\\\\n51:## 2. 四个必须停下来的人工锁点\\\\n52:\\\\n53:除非用户已经明确授权连续执行，否则以下节点必须显式确认后再继续：\\\\n54:\\\\n55:1. **Story Lock**：故事与专业分镜是否锁定。\\\\n56:2. **Visual Lock**：三张真实性校准与四张视觉准入是否锁定。\\\\n57:3. **Repair Lock**：需要返修哪些图；未点名已通过帧不得连带重做。\\\\n58:4. **Release Lock**：标题、封面、字幕、简介、话题、发布图是否为最终版。\\\\n59:\\\\n60:这四个锁点不是新状态机，只是人工决策 Gate。\\\\n61:\\\\n62:## 3. Visual Baseline → Trial → Batch\\\\n63:\\\\n64:所有新篇统一使用：\\\\n65:\\\\n66:```text\\\\n67:人物 / 场景 / 设备真实性基线\\\\n68:→ 三张真实性校准\\\\n69:   A. 普通相册基线\\\\n70:   B. 最差但仍成立条件\\\\n71:   C. 首次重大异常\\\\n72:→ 四张视觉准入帧\\\\n73:→ VISUAL_CALIBRATED\\\\n74:→ 剩余图片批量生产\\\\n75:```\\\\n76:\\\\n77:禁止“先把 20 张都出完，再回头找画风”。\\\\n78:\\\\n79:## 4. 最小修改协议\\\\n80:\\\\n81:用户说：\\\\n82:\\\\n83:- “只改字幕 / 底图别动” → `subtitle_only`\\\\n84:- “只裁切” → `crop_only`\\\\n85:- “保持原画风重做这一张” → `regenerate_frame`\\\\n86:- “整段重做” → `regenerate_sequence`\\\\n87:\\\\n88:未被点名的已通过帧默认锁定，不得顺手重做。\\\\n89:\\\\n90:## 5. 一条命令知道下一步\\\\n91:\\\\n92:```bash\\\\n93:python episodes/_system/story_os.py next <episode_dir>\\\\n94:```\\\\n95:\\\\n96:仓库健康检查：\\\\n97:\\\\n98:```bash\\\\n99:python episodes/_system/story_os.py doctor\\\\n100:```\\\\n101:\\\\n102:生成最终验收清单：\\\\n103:\\\\n104:```bash\\\\n105:python episodes/_system/story_os.py checklist <episode_dir>\\\\n106:```\\\\n107:\\\\n108:只看状态，不修改：\\\\n109:\\\\n110:```bash\\\\n111:python episodes/_system/story_os.py status <episode_dir>\\\\n112:```\\\\n113:\\\\n114:## 6. 文档权威规则\\\\n115:\\\\n116:`standards/AUTHORITY_INDEX.json` 只做路由，不创造规则：\\\\n117:\\\\n118:- `canonical`：唯一主规范。\\\\n119:- `active_subordinate`：当前有效执行细则。\\\\n120:- `series_overlay`：系列覆盖层，只能补充，不得反向覆盖主规范硬规则。\\\\n121:- `reference`：参考材料，不是门禁。\\\\n122:- `superseded`：历史版本，默认禁止作为当前规则引用。\\\\n123:\\\\n124:出现冲突：\\\\n125:\\\\n126:```text\\\\n127:制作规范_正式版\\\\n128:> active subordinate\\\\n129:> series overlay\\\\n130:> reference\\\\n131:> superseded\\\\n132:```\\\\n133:\\\\n134:## 7. Final QA 只生成，不再造第五套规范\\\\n135:\\\\n136:`final_checklist.py` 只从现有状态、门禁和 manifest 汇总一份：\\\\n137:\\\\n138:`<episode>/meta/FINAL_CHECKLIST.md`\\\\n139:\\\\n140:它不是规范源，也不得保存 stage。最终人工仍需回答：\\\\n141:\\\\n142:- 像不像真实手机相册 / 合理采集设备？\\\\n143:- 人物、地点、关键道具是否连续？\\\\n144:- 前 5 张有没有继续滑的欲望？\\\\n145:- 高潮是否足够强，且不是近期作品的重复机制？\\\\n146:- 结尾是否回收前文，并产生回看价值？\\\\n147:- 字幕是否像人话、位置是否压住主体？\\\\n148:- 封面 / 标题 / 简介 / 话题是否和成片一致？\\\\n149:\\\\n150:## 8. 一句话原则\\\\n151:\\\\n152:**规则可以很多，决策入口只能有一个。**\\\\n153:\\\\n154:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_7_RELIABILITY_BEGIN -->\\\\n155:## 9. V1.7 生产可靠性\\\\n156:\\\\n157:Golden Path 七阶段不变。V1.7 只在两个位置增加事务保护：\\\\n158:\\\\n159:```text\\\\n160:Batch 生图请求\\\\n161:→ production_ledger begin\\\\n162:→ transport_guard preflight\\\\n163:→ 调用生图\\\\n164:→ success / technical failure\\\\n165:\\\\n166:已锁图片只修文字\\\\n167:→ text_revision start\\\\n168:→ 编辑\\\\n169:→ diff + text_audit\\\\n170:→ submit\\\\n171:→ 用户明确批准 approve / 不满意 revert\\\\n172:```\\\\n173:\\\\n174:技术失败不得消耗内容返修次数；技术重试不得改变请求指纹。文字专修不得触碰批准/发布图片、reference、release manifest、production ledger、episode state 或 story gates。\\\\n175:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_7_RELIABILITY_END -->\\\\n176:\\\\n177:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_8_DEFAULT_STYLE_BEGIN -->\\\\n178:## 10. V1.8 默认视觉 IP 与三道不可漂移锁\\\\n179:\\\\n180:用户没有明确指定画风/质感时，默认解析：\\\\n181:\\\\n182:`M00｜MP4 × 网吧 × 流水席旧数码质感校准版`\\\\n183:\\\\n184:但它只统一视觉语言；**本集年代和实际采集设备的物理表现优先**，禁止把现代手机硬做成旧低清设备。\\\\n185:\\\\n186:V1.8 不新增 episode stage，只给现有 Golden Path 增加证据锁：\\\\n187:\\\\n188:```text\\\\n189:Story Lock → story + storyboard approval SHA\\\\n190:Visual Lock → visual spec + calibration + references + resolved profile SHA\\\\n191:Batch → 现有 V1.7 production / transport\\\\n192:Text Audit → text-audit.json 必须 PASS 且 captions SHA 不漂移\\\\n193:Release → release-package.json 锁最终封面/正文/字幕/发布文案/传播卡 SHA\\\\n194:```\\\\n195:\\\\n196:常用命令：\\\\n197:\\\\n198:```bash\\\\n199:python episodes/_system/story_os.py visual-profile <episode_dir> show\\\\n200:python episodes/_system/story_os.py approval <episode_dir> story --user-approved\\\\n201:python episodes/_system/story_os.py approval <episode_dir> visual --user-approved\\\\n202:python episodes/_system/story_os.py audit-text <episode_dir>\\\\n203:python episodes/_system/story_os.py release-package <episode_dir> build --user-approved\\\\n204:```\\\\n205:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_8_DEFAULT_STYLE_END -->\\\\n206:\\\\n207:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_MULTI_RUNTIME_BEGIN -->\\\\n208:## 11. V2.0 Multi-Runtime\\\\n209:\\\\n210:启动时按 `runtimes/runtime-contract.json` 自动判断执行环境，不询问用户选择模式：\\\\n211:\\\\n212:`可写仓库+terminal/code execution → CODEX；ChatGPT Work → WORK；其他普通 ChatGPT → WEB`\\\\n213:\\\\n214:三个 runtime 只改变执行方式，不改变创作权威和 episode stage。\\\\n215:\\\\n216:用户明确说“全自动执行 / 一次做完 / 做到最终交付 / 不要每步问我”时，视为连续执行授权。正常 Golden Path 不重复询问是否继续；自动审查必须标记为 delegated_auto_review，不得写成用户亲眼审核。\\\\n217:\\\\n218:统一恢复证据：`<episode>/meta/runtime-checkpoint.json`。它不是 stage。\\\\n219:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_MULTI_RUNTIME_END -->\\\\n220:\\\\n221:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_1_ENGINEERING_BEGIN -->\\\\n222:## 12. V2.0.1 工程补强\\\\n223:\\\\n224:CODEX runtime 新增一键入口：\\\\n225:\\\\n226:```bash\\\\n227:python episodes/_system/story_os.py run <episode_dir> --full-auto\\\\n228:```\\\\n229:\\\\n230:它使用当前 Codex CLI 登录态启动独立全自动 worker；正式图片可通过 `codex_subscription_image.py` 落成真实文件，不要求 API Key。全自动审查统一记为 `delegated_auto_review`，不得伪造 `direct_user_review` 或 Release Lock。\\\\n231:\\\\n232:证据门禁外部稳定名统一为 `evidence_gate.py`；`v18_gate.py` 只作为历史兼容实现保留。\\\\n233:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_1_ENGINEERING_END -->\\\\n234:\\\\n235:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_2_CLOSURE_BEGIN -->\\\\n236:## Story OS V2.0.2 Production Closure\\\\n237:\\\\n238:CODEX 全自动完成必须经过 deterministic postflight；worker 正常退出不等于完成。生图必须使用 `generate-for-frame` 走 raw→canvas normalize→ledger。全自动 Story/Visual/Release 使用 delegated approval 证据，不伪造用户亲审。最终 delegated ZIP 禁止 approved fallback，必须包含真实 publish 资产和完整文本/manifest/hash。\\\\n239:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_2_CLOSURE_END -->\\\\n240:\\\\n241:\\\\n242:## V2.0.3.3 Frame Semantic Enforcement\\\\n243:\\\\n244:Batch 完成后，`PRODUCTION_PASSED` 前必须运行 `episodes/_system/frame_semantic_review.py` 的 fresh isolated full-frame-set critic；实际图片必须与 Story Lock / Storyboard / Authenticity Card / Continuity Anchors 一致，并通过 SHA-bound review 与 near-duplicate audit。该证据不新增机器状态。\\\\n245:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_3_4_INCREMENTAL_WORKSPACE_BEGIN -->\\\\n246:## V2.0.3.4 最小闭环 + 本地媒体工作区\\\\n247:\\\\n248:默认先做增量计划，不再无条件重跑整篇：\\\\n249:\\\\n250:```bash\\\\n251:python episodes/_system/incremental_closure.py plan <episode_dir> --json\\\\n252:```\\\\n253:\\\\n254:帧审核统一入口：\\\\n255:\\\\n256:```bash\\\\n257:python episodes/_system/incremental_frame_review.py review <episode_dir> --attempt 1\\\\n258:```\\\\n259:\\\\n260:- CLEAN 的 Story / Visual / Frame 证据按 SHA 直接复用。\\\\n261:- 只改 1~N 张图时默认审核 dirty frame ±1；终局高风险帧默认 ±2。\\\\n262:- Story / Storyboard / Visual Contract 改变，或 dirty > 25%，自动升级 FULL_FRAME_SET。\\\\n263:- 全局 SHA、尺寸、近重复仍执行廉价全量审计。\\\\n264:\\\\n265:新篇本地媒体统一放：`media/calibration|raw|candidates|approved|publish|review|archive`；交付放 `release/`；Git 只跟踪 `meta/media-index.json` 与文本/证据，不跟踪这些像素资产。\\\\n266:\\\\n267:媒体工具：\\\\n268:\\\\n269:```bash\\\\n270:python episodes/_system/media_workspace.py inventory\\\\n271:python episodes/_system/media_workspace.py migrate --dry-run\\\\n272:python episodes/_system/media_workspace.py ensure <episode_dir>\\\\n273:```\\\\n274:\\\\n275:历史未纳管 episode 不自动搬图；重新进入制作时再迁移。\\\\n276:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_3_4_INCREMENTAL_WORKSPACE_END -->\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\r\\nepisodes/10_山难伪纪录片/01_鳌太线_热汤/media/review\\\\manual-production-04-face-check.jsonl:167:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.cache\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\native\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pwsh.exe\\\\\\\" -Command 'rg -n \\\\\\\"''^\\\\\\\" '\\\\\\\"'C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\skills\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\douyin-horror-story-pipeline\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\SKILL.md'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"1:---\\\\n2:name: douyin-horror-story-pipeline\\\\n3:description: Bilingual production workflow for Douyin AI horror/storytelling image posts. Use when the user sends “选题”, “分镜”, “验收”, “自动”, or “对比打分”, or asks to design, storyboard, audit, score, or compare a first-person suspense image-story project using the 鼠鼠传播节奏 + Zayn视觉扩张 mixed mode.\\\\n4:---\\\\n5:\\\\n6:# Douyin Horror Story Pipeline\\\\n7:\\\\n8:Use this skill to run a structured, bilingual-capable production pipeline for first-person Douyin suspense/horror image stories. The default project language is Chinese; answer in English when the user explicitly requests English or sends an English command. Keep Chinese command names and S/Z labels unchanged in both languages.\\\\n9:\\\\n10:## Authority and references\\\\n11:\\\\n12:For work inside `aigc-dali-cat`, read the repository authority documents before making judgments:\\\\n13:\\\\n14:- `standards/制作规范_正式版.md`\\\\n15:- The relevant episode `README.md`, docs, assets README, storyboard, publish checklist, and review files\\\\n16:- `shushu/` and `zayn/` only when competitor-sample evidence is needed; treat them as local samples, not universal platform rules\\\\n17:\\\\n18:Load the detailed language reference only as needed:\\\\n19:\\\\n20:- Chinese workflow: `references/zh-CN.md`\\\\n21:- English workflow: `references/en-US.md`\\\\n22:\\\\n23:Do not invent missing source facts. Mark assumptions as assumptions. Preserve the distinction between a design score, a pre-publish acceptance score, and live platform performance.\\\\n24:\\\\n25:## Command router\\\\n26:\\\\n27:Detect the first command token. Ignore surrounding punctuation, whitespace, and a trailing colon.\\\\n28:\\\\n29:| User command | Mode | Required behavior |\\\\n30:|---|---|---|\\\\n31:| `选题：` / `topic:` | Structure only | Produce story structure; do not write the full storyboard, generate images, or claim acceptance. |\\\\n32:| `分镜：` / `storyboard:` | Storyboard | Build the storyboard from an approved or supplied structure; do not silently change the premise. |\\\\n33:| `验收：` / `acceptance:` | Acceptance | Inspect supplied artifacts and report pass/fail, blockers, and minimum fixes; do not rewrite unless asked. |\\\\n34:| `自动：` / `auto:` | Full pipeline | Run structure → storyboard → acceptance in order. Stop at a blocking failure and report what must be fixed. Do not generate images or publish unless explicitly requested. |\\\\n35:| `对比打分：` / `compare score:` | Directory comparison | Require a directory path. The directory must contain at least one of topic/structure, storyboard, or images. Compare all available components across multiple dimensions and score with evidence. |\\\\n36:\\\\n37:If no command is recognizable, explain the five commands briefly and ask the user to prefix the task with one. For `对比打分` without a directory, ask for the directory and do not score from memory. For a directory with no recognized topic/storyboard/image evidence, report insufficient evidence and request the missing path or artifact.\\\\n38:\\\\n39:## Non-negotiable mixed-mode rules\\\\n40:\\\\n41:The default mode is:\\\\n42:\\\\n43:`节奏模式：混合模式（鼠鼠主行动 + Zayn视觉扩张）`\\\\n44:\\\\n45:Mixed mode is not a third independent rhythm. It requires both causal systems:\\\\n46:\\\\n47:- 鼠鼠 S1-S8: everyday task, emotional anchor, relationship guide, visible anomaly, rule, transgression, physical confrontation, human closure, and aftermath.\\\\n48:- Zayn Z1-Z8: credible entry, motif shown by image 3, same-source recurrence, rule confirmation, character involvement, scale expansion, event closure, and ending re-read.\\\\n49:\\\\n50:Hard constraints:\\\\n51:\\\\n52:- Default 20 images; maximum 25.\\\\n53:- Image 3 must show a concrete, directly visible anomaly.\\\\n54:- The first three images must establish real-world motivation/relationship pressure and the anomaly.\\\\n55:- Define one anomaly motif as `core form + material/color + motion/growth/mimicry rule`.\\\\n56:- Use at least three different carriers and three scales; each recurrence must add a new inference.\\\\n57:- The character must act, not only observe; the real task and relationship must close.\\\\n58:- The final image must provide physical aftermath and change the meaning of at least two earlier images.\\\\n59:- Do not use “未完待续” to avoid closure.\\\\n60:- Do not copy competitor characters, entities, shots, dialogue, or distinctive designs.\\\\n61:\\\\n62:Realism guardrails (提炼自 oh-my-folkstoryphoto，适配本项目现有节奏与目录):\\\\n63:\\\\n64:- Every new episode must add a short `真实性方案` section to its existing `docs/` topic or storyboard document before image handoff: primary capture device, photographer, why the device is present, 9:16 capture behavior, and stable/restricted/out-of-control image states.\\\\n65:- Before the full image handoff, run a three-shot visual calibration using the existing P0/四图准入 workflow: ordinary baseline, worst capture condition, and first major anomaly. These are review checkpoints, not extra publish images; approved calibration frames may be reused as the corresponding final frames.\\\\n66:- Treat viewpoint physics, unplanned recorder/device visibility, capture-profile continuity, and non-cinematic drift as hard acceptance checks. A prompt request alone is not evidence; inspect the returned image when available.\\\\n67:- Record the calibration result and the approved storyboard/version hash in the episode's existing `docs/` review file. Do not create a parallel state machine or new project directory.\\\\n68:- Content repair is one round per image. Keep the original candidate and repair decision in the existing episode version directory; a second hard failure is `不通过`/`needs_user`, never silently accepted.\\\\n69:\\\\n70:## Mode behavior\\\\n71:\\\\n72:### `选题` / `topic`\\\\n73:\\\\n74:Read the relevant authority docs, then output only: premise, location, protagonist, real task, emotional anchor, relationship character, anomaly motif, controversy hooks, title candidates with scores, S1-S8, Z1-Z8, motif carriers/scales, proposed 20-image beat map, risks, and a go/no-go structure verdict. Do not output the full per-image prompt set.\\\\n75:\\\\n76:### `分镜` / `storyboard`\\\\n77:\\\\n78:Require an approved structure or clearly supplied premise. Output each image’s act, S/Z labels, function, visual content, first-person method, characters/props, caption, caption function, motif carrier, scale, causal link, generation prompt, negative prompt, and continuity risk. Do not add unapproved major lore. Finish with asset-lock and caption checks.\\\\n79:\\\\n80:### `验收` / `acceptance`\\\\n81:\\\\n82:Inspect the supplied text and image artifacts. For images, use visual inspection when available; never mark visual consistency from filenames alone. Classify findings as `必须重出`, `必须改文`, `建议调整`, or `可接受`. Check S/Z completeness, first-three hook, motif recurrence, scale progression, first-person framing, character/prop continuity, captions, closure, originality, and publish readiness. A score is not a pass if a hard blocker remains.\\\\n83:\\\\n84:### `自动` / `auto`\\\\n85:\\\\n86:Run the three modes sequentially. Preserve approved decisions between stages. If structure fails, do not continue to storyboard. If storyboard fails, do not claim acceptance. If acceptance finds blockers, return the minimum repair list and the final status `有条件通过` or `不通过`. Image generation is a separate action and requires an explicit request.\\\\n87:\\\\n88:### `对比打分` / `compare score`\\\\n89:\\\\n90:Require an explicit directory. Inspect every relevant file under it, recognizing Chinese/English filenames and common Markdown/image formats. The directory must contain one or more of:\\\\n91:\\\\n92:- topic/structure evidence;\\\\n93:- storyboard evidence;\\\\n94:- image evidence.\\\\n95:\\\\n96:Compare available entries or versions, never pretend absent components exist. Use these dimensions, scoring each 0-10 with file/image evidence:\\\\n97:\\\\n98:1. topic hook and everyday entry;\\\\n99:2. S1-S8 causal completeness;\\\\n100:3. Z1-Z8 motif/scale completeness;\\\\n101:4. first-three retention potential;\\\\n102:5. narrative causality and information change;\\\\n103:6. emotional/relationship closure;\\\\n104:7. ending aftermath and re-read;\\\\n105:8. motif continuity and originality;\\\\n106:9. first-person visual realism;\\\\n107:10. character, prop, and scene consistency;\\\\n108:11. caption usability and obstruction risk;\\\\n109:12. production readiness and acceptance risk.\\\\n110:\\\\n111:For each candidate, provide a score table, evidence, weaknesses, confidence, and a ranked recommendation. If only images exist, do not infer the full story causality or captions; mark those dimensions `未提供证据` and exclude them from the normalized total. If only documents exist, do not claim image quality. Use a weighted total only after stating which dimensions were actually scored.\\\\n112:\\\\n113:## Output discipline\\\\n114:\\\\n115:Lead with the verdict. Keep evidence tied to paths and image numbers. Separate facts, inferences, and missing evidence. Do not alter repository files, rewrite story documents, or create images unless the user explicitly asks for that action. When this skill does produce or edit artifacts, finish with:\\\\n116:\\\\n117:`【目标】 【改动文件】 【自测结果】 【风险】 【必须验收】 【结论】`\\\\n118:\\\\n119:## Language selection\\\\n120:\\\\n121:Use `references/zh-CN.md` for Chinese output and `references/en-US.md` for English output. The two references define the same workflow and acceptance gates; keep labels `鼠鼠节奏-S1~S8` and `Zayn节奏-Z1~Z8` alongside translated explanations.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\r\\nepisodes/10_山难伪纪录片/01_鳌太线_热汤/media/review\\\\manual-production-04-face-check.jsonl:186:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.cache\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\native\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pwsh.exe\\\\\\\" -Command 'rg -n \\\\\\\"''^\\\\\\\" SKILL.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"1:# Dali Cat Story OS — Repository Execution Contract V2.0.3.4\\\\n2:\\\\n3:> 这是 `aigc-dali-cat/story` 的 Agent 执行入口，不是第二套创作规范。\\\\n4:> **创作规则冲突时，以 `standards/制作规范_正式版.md` 为唯一权威。**\\\\n5:> **机器阶段冲突时，以 `meta/episode-state.json` 为唯一状态事实源。**\\\\n6:\\\\n7:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_6_GOLDEN_PATH_BEGIN -->\\\\n8:## Story OS V2.0.3.4 Golden Path\\\\n9:\\\\n10:**第一入口：先读 `START_HERE.md`。** 该文件只负责路由，不建立第二套创作规范。\\\\n11:\\\\n12:Golden Path：`选题/去同质化 → Story Lock → 真实性卡/连续性锚点 → 三张校准+四张视觉准入 → Visual Lock → Batch → 逐帧审核/必要返修 → Final Checklist → Release → 数据回填`。\\\\n13:\\\\n14:- 创作规则唯一权威仍是 `standards/制作规范_正式版.md`。\\\\n15:- 阶段唯一事实源仍是 `meta/episode-state.json`。\\\\n16:- `AUTHORITY_INDEX.json / story-gates / production-ledger / frame-reviews / FINAL_CHECKLIST` 都只是路由或证据，不得成为第二状态机。\\\\n17:- 不要默认通读整个 `standards/`；按 `standards/AUTHORITY_INDEX.json` 只读取当前任务需要的 active 细则。\\\\n18:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_6_GOLDEN_PATH_END -->\\\\n19:\\\\n20:## 1. 单一状态源\\\\n21:\\\\n22:禁止再创建第二套 `episode.yaml stage`。\\\\n23:\\\\n24:每篇接入机器状态的剧集使用：\\\\n25:\\\\n26:```text\\\\n27:meta/\\\\n28:├── episode-state.json       # 唯一阶段状态源\\\\n29:├── release-manifest.json    # 最终发布版本事实\\\\n30:├── story-gates.json         # 故事/视觉/字幕/锁图/机器证据配置，不保存阶段\\\\n31:├── production-ledger.json   # 逐帧生产事务，不保存阶段\\\\n32:└── frame-reviews/           # 严格模式下逐帧真实性结构化审查\\\\n33:```\\\\n34:\\\\n35:职责必须分离：\\\\n36:\\\\n37:- `episode-state.json`：只回答“现在处于哪个阶段”。\\\\n38:- `release-manifest.json`：只回答“最终准备/实际发布的是哪一版”。\\\\n39:- `story-gates.json`：只回答“进入下一阶段所需证据是否齐全”。\\\\n40:- `production-ledger.json`：只回答“每张图生产过程发生了什么”。\\\\n41:- `frame-reviews/NN.json`：只回答“该帧真实性/连续性硬项是否通过”。\\\\n42:\\\\n43:任何证据文件都不能覆盖 `current_state`，也不能自建另一套 stage。\\\\n44:\\\\n45:## 2. 任务开始前必须读取\\\\n46:\\\\n47:读取顺序只由 `START_HERE.md` 第 1 节维护，本文件不再复制第二份顺序。执行到本文件后，继续按 `AGENTS.md → standards/制作规范_正式版.md → AUTHORITY_INDEX.json active 细则 → 目标剧集` 路由。`README.md` 只做项目说明，不是执行入口。\\\\n48:\\\\n49:## 3. 唯一生产状态机\\\\n50:\\\\n51:沿用仓库原生 `_system`：\\\\n52:\\\\n53:```text\\\\n54:IDEA_LOCKED\\\\n55:→ STORYBOARD_LOCKED\\\\n56:→ VISUAL_CALIBRATED\\\\n57:→ PRODUCTION_PASSED\\\\n58:→ PUBLISH_READY\\\\n59:→ PUBLISHED\\\\n60:→ DATA_REVIEWED\\\\n61:```\\\\n62:\\\\n63:正向推进必须使用：\\\\n64:\\\\n65:```bash\\\\n66:python episodes/_system/episode_state.py transition <episode_dir> <TARGET> --note \\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\"\\\\n67:```\\\\n68:\\\\n69:当前正向推进会依次执行：\\\\n70:\\\\n71:1. `validate_episode.py`：manifest / 发布条件门禁；\\\\n72:2. `machine_gate.py`：真实性、校准、参考资产、逐帧结构化审查、production ledger 硬门禁；\\\\n73:3. `evidence_gate.py`：Story / Visual / Release 的稳定审批 provenance 与 SHA 门禁。\\\\n74:\\\\n75:任一失败不得推进。禁止手改 `current_state` 越级。\\\\n76:\\\\n77:## 4. Story OS 门禁映射\\\\n78:\\\\n79:### STORY_GATE → 进入 STORYBOARD_LOCKED 前\\\\n80:\\\\n81:必须满足：\\\\n82:\\\\n83:- 最近 5 篇账号级同质化检查完成\\\\n84:- 四把锁至少 2 把不同\\\\n85:- 未触发机制换皮一票否决\\\\n86:- 任务/事件闭环\\\\n87:- 至少保留 2 种竞争解释\\\\n88:- hook / climax / payoff 已明确\\\\n89:- `reviews.story = passed`\\\\n90:\\\\n91:### VISUAL_GATE → 进入 VISUAL_CALIBRATED 前\\\\n92:\\\\n93:原有门禁：\\\\n94:\\\\n95:- 恰好 4 张视觉准入帧，图号合法且互不重复\\\\n96:- `reviews.visual_admission = passed`\\\\n97:- `reviews.authenticity = passed`\\\\n98:- `continuity.required` 中声明的连续性锚点全部填写\\\\n99:- 不允许“先批量出图，再补锚点”\\\\n100:\\\\n101:V1.5 严格机器门禁追加：\\\\n102:\\\\n103:- 项目级真实性卡完整：年代、地点、拍摄者、拍摄原因、主设备、稳定/受限/失控三种状态\\\\n104:- 辅助采集设备最多 2 种且必须有剧情来源\\\\n105:- 当前第一视角设备或拍摄者若完整入镜，必须登记物理解释\\\\n106:- 三张校准必须分别为：普通相册基线 / 最差但成立条件 / 首次重大异常\\\\n107:- 三张校准必须是三个不同图号，且属于四张视觉准入帧\\\\n108:- 三张校准资产和联系表必须保存 SHA-256 并保持不变\\\\n109:- 若本集声明 `references.required=true`，所有 required anchors 都必须有已通过且 hash 锁定的 reference asset\\\\n110:\\\\n111:### PRODUCTION_GATE → 进入 PRODUCTION_PASSED 前\\\\n112:\\\\n113:原有门禁：\\\\n114:\\\\n115:- `reviews.production = passed`\\\\n116:- `reviews.continuity = passed`\\\\n117:- `reviews.authenticity = passed`\\\\n118:- 若本集需要字幕：声音卡完成、`reviews.subtitle = passed`、captions 证据存在\\\\n119:\\\\n120:V1.5 严格机器门禁追加：\\\\n121:\\\\n122:- `production-ledger.json` 正文帧数必须等于 manifest\\\\n123:- 每帧状态必须为 `PASSED` 或 `LOCKED`\\\\n124:- 每帧最多一次内容返修\\\\n125:- 每帧必须有 approved asset + SHA-256\\\\n126:- `LOCKED` 帧的 lock hash 必须等于 approved asset hash\\\\n127:- 每帧必须有 `meta/frame-reviews/NN.json`\\\\n128:- `viewpoint_physics / capture_profile_match / not_cinematic / album_test` 必须 pass\\\\n129:- identity / key_prop / location / continuity 等字段只要出现 fail 即阻断\\\\n130:- 有效摄影红旗 >=3 即阻断\\\\n131:- 红旗豁免必须是 detected 的子集且有预登记原因\\\\n132:- `repair / must_regenerate` 不得进入 PRODUCTION_PASSED\\\\n133:\\\\n134:### RELEASE_GATE → 进入 PUBLISH_READY 前\\\\n135:\\\\n136:在原传播评分/发布 Manifest 门禁基础上增加：\\\\n137:\\\\n138:- `reviews.recommendation_fit = passed`\\\\n139:- `reviews.publish = passed`\\\\n140:- publish 正文数量符合 `body_frame_count`\\\\n141:- 本地完整验收时，正文发布图必须匹配 manifest 画幅：4:5 → 1080×1350；9:16 → 1080×1920；新篇未指定时默认 4:5\\\\n142:- 锁定底图 SHA-256 不得变化\\\\n143:\\\\n144:## 5. 最小修改协议\\\\n145:\\\\n146:用户修改指令默认解释为最小改动：\\\\n147:\\\\n148:- “只改字幕 / 底图别动 / 一像素尽量别动” → `locks.edit_mode = subtitle_only`\\\\n149:- “只裁切” → `crop_only`\\\\n150:- “保持原画风重做这一张” → `regenerate_frame`\\\\n151:- “整段重做” → `regenerate_sequence`\\\\n152:\\\\n153:当 `subtitle_only`：\\\\n154:\\\\n155:- `locks.assets` 至少登记 1 个底图\\\\n156:- 必须保存 SHA-256\\\\n157:- 本地 validator 发现任一锁定资产 hash 改变立即 FAIL\\\\n158:- 未点名的已通过帧不得连带重做\\\\n159:\\\\n160:## 5.1 Production Engine V1.2\\\\n161:\\\\n162:正式出图使用 `meta/production-ledger.json` 记录逐帧请求指纹、技术失败、内容返修、候选 SHA-256、approved/lock 资产与批次；它不得保存剧集 stage。\\\\n163:\\\\n164:- 未指定画幅：默认 `4:5 / 1080×1350`。\\\\n165:- 明确指定 `9:16`：使用 `1080×1920`。\\\\n166:- 技术失败不占内容返修次数；每帧最多一次内容返修。\\\\n167:- originals / repairs / approved / publish 必须分离，不得覆盖原图。\\\\n168:- 正式请求默认 prompt ≤260 字符且 ≤900 UTF-8 bytes，reference 默认最多 2 张并记录 role/kind/hash。\\\\n169:- 详细执行见 `standards/生产引擎与画幅规范_V1.2.md` 和 `episodes/_system/production_ledger.py`。\\\\n170:\\\\n171:## 5.2 Machine Evidence V1.5\\\\n172:\\\\n173:机器化不负责替代审美判断，只负责把已经写进规范的“硬条件”变成可验证证据。\\\\n174:\\\\n175:常用命令：\\\\n176:\\\\n177:```bash\\\\n178:# 新篇初始化后创建逐帧审查模板\\\\n179:python episodes/_system/evidence_tool.py init-reviews <episode_dir>\\\\n180:\\\\n181:# 把已完成的真实性卡写回 story-gates\\\\n182:python episodes/_system/evidence_tool.py import-authenticity <episode_dir> --file <card.json>\\\\n183:\\\\n184:# 锁三张校准\\\\n185:python episodes/_system/evidence_tool.py record-calibration <episode_dir> --role baseline --frame 01 --asset <01.png> --decision passed\\\\n186:python episodes/_system/evidence_tool.py record-calibration <episode_dir> --role worst_condition --frame 10 --asset <10.png> --decision passed\\\\n187:python episodes/_system/evidence_tool.py record-calibration <episode_dir> --role first_major_anomaly --frame 04 --asset <04.png> --decision passed\\\\n188:\\\\n189:# 生成三张校准联系表并写回 hash\\\\n190:python episodes/_system/calibration_sheet.py <episode_dir>\\\\n191:\\\\n192:# 连续性参考资产（仅需要时）\\\\n193:python episodes/_system/evidence_tool.py reference-policy <episode_dir> --required --anchor protagonist --anchor location\\\\n194:python episodes/_system/evidence_tool.py register-reference <episode_dir> --id protagonist-main --anchor protagonist --kind identity --asset <ref.png>\\\\n195:\\\\n196:# 最终机器预检\\\\n197:python episodes/_system/machine_gate.py <episode_dir> --target PRODUCTION_PASSED\\\\n198:```\\\\n199:\\\\n200:## 6. 新篇初始化 / 旧篇升级\\\\n201:\\\\n202:新篇：\\\\n203:\\\\n204:```bash\\\\n205:python episodes/_system/episode_state.py init \\\\\\\\\\\\n206:  episodes/10_新系列/01_新故事 \\\\\\\\\\\\n207:  --id 10-01 \\\\\\\\\\\\n208:  --series 10_新系列 \\\\\\\\\\\\n209:  --title \\\\\\\"新故事\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\n210:  --frame-count 20\\\\n211:```\\\\n212:\\\\n213:V1.5 新篇默认 `machine_contract.strict=true`，不允许缺真实性机器证据进入后续阶段。\\\\n214:\\\\n215:旧剧集不批量伪造证据。缺 `story-gates.json` 时先：\\\\n216:\\\\n217:```bash\\\\n218:python episodes/_system/episode_state.py migrate-gates <episode_dir>\\\\n219:```\\\\n220:\\\\n221:迁移后默认 `machine_contract.strict=false`。只有旧剧集重新进入制作且真实证据已准备时执行：\\\\n222:\\\\n223:```bash\\\\n224:python episodes/_system/episode_state.py enable-machine-gates <episode_dir>\\\\n225:```\\\\n226:\\\\n227:该命令只开启严格验证，不会自动把任何 review 标记为 passed。\\\\n228:\\\\n229:## 7. 验收\\\\n230:\\\\n231:原 Story OS：\\\\n232:\\\\n233:```bash\\\\n234:python episodes/_system/validate_episode.py <episode_dir>\\\\n235:python episodes/_system/validate_episode.py <episode_dir> --target VISUAL_CALIBRATED\\\\n236:python episodes/_system/validate_episode.py --all --metadata-only\\\\n237:```\\\\n238:\\\\n239:机器证据：\\\\n240:\\\\n241:```bash\\\\n242:python episodes/_system/machine_gate.py <episode_dir> --target VISUAL_CALIBRATED\\\\n243:python episodes/_system/machine_gate.py <episode_dir> --target PRODUCTION_PASSED\\\\n244:python episodes/_system/machine_gate.py --all --metadata-only\\\\n245:```\\\\n246:\\\\n247:本地正式推进不要使用 `--metadata-only`。\\\\n248:\\\\n249:## 8. 边界\\\\n250:\\\\n251:机器门禁可以判断“证据是否齐、图片尺寸/数量/hash 是否正确、硬失败字段是否存在”，但不能替代人工/多模态判断：\\\\n252:\\\\n253:- 是否真实像手机相册\\\\n254:- 是否有继续滑动欲望\\\\n255:- 人物是否像同一个人\\\\n256:- 高潮是否真正够强\\\\n257:- 结尾是否产生回看价值\\\\n258:\\\\n259:这些仍必须按主规范人工终审。机器只负责：**人工已经做过判断后，不允许证据缺失、状态漂移或返工越界。**\\\\n260:\\\\n261:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_7_RELIABILITY_BEGIN -->\\\\n262:## Story OS V1.7 — Production Reliability\\\\n263:\\\\n264:V1.7 不新增 episode stage，只增加生产可靠性证据与文字专修事务：\\\\n265:\\\\n266:- `episodes/_system/transport_guard.py`：技术重试请求指纹锁、失败分类、熔断；技术失败不计内容返修。\\\\n267:- `episodes/_system/text_audit.py`：字幕硬项 + AI 腔警告，只审计不自动改稿。\\\\n268:- `episodes/_system/text_revision.py`：文字专修 backup → diff → audit → submit → approve/revert；锁定图片/reference/manifest/state 不得变化。\\\\n269:- `meta/transport-state.json` 与 `meta/text-revisions/` 都是证据/事务，不是第二状态机。\\\\n270:\\\\n271:常用入口：\\\\n272:\\\\n273:```bash\\\\n274:python episodes/_system/story_os.py transport <episode_dir> preflight <frame>\\\\n275:python episodes/_system/story_os.py audit-text <episode_dir> --file <subtitles.yaml>\\\\n276:python episodes/_system/story_os.py text-revision <episode_dir> start --file <path>\\\\n277:```\\\\n278:\\\\n279:详细执行见 `standards/生产可靠性与文本事务规范_V1.0.md`。\\\\n280:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_7_RELIABILITY_END -->\\\\n281:\\\\n282:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_8_EVIDENCE_BEGIN -->\\\\n283:## Story OS V1.8 — Default Visual IP + Evidence Locks\\\\n284:\\\\n285:- 用户未指定画风/质感：默认 `M00｜MP4 × 网吧 × 流水席旧数码质感校准版`。\\\\n286:- 显式单集/系列风格可覆盖默认 M00；年代/设备物理真实性永远高于母风格“复古感”。\\\\n287:- Story Lock 必须保存 story + storyboard 的明确批准和 SHA-256。\\\\n288:- Visual Lock 必须保存 visual spec、校准联系表、已通过 reference 与解析后 visual profile 的明确批准和 SHA-256。\\\\n289:- `PUBLISH_READY` 前必须有最新 `meta/text-audit.json`，且其 `source_sha256` 等于当前 captions。\\\\n290:- `PUBLISH_READY` 前必须有用户明确批准的 `meta/release-package.json`，最终封面/正文/字幕/发布文案/传播卡 hash 全部一致。\\\\n291:- V1.7 的 transport guard / text revision transaction 原样保留，不重复造轮子。\\\\n292:<!-- STORY_OS_V1_8_EVIDENCE_END -->\\\\n293:\\\\n294:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_MULTI_RUNTIME_SKILL_BEGIN -->\\\\n295:## Story OS V2.0 Multi-Runtime Execution\\\\n296:\\\\n297:- CODEX：文件原生全自动生产，目标 approved/publish/SHA/FINAL ZIP。\\\\n298:- WORK：持久工作区长任务，目标一次任务尽量做到最终交付。\\\\n299:- WEB：尽量连续执行；产品工具边界出现时写 checkpoint，下一轮直接恢复。\\\\n300:\\\\n301:用户已明确授权“全自动”时，不在正常 Story/Visual/Repair/Release 节点重复询问“是否继续”；只在硬冲突、权限/安全确认、一次内容返修后仍失败等情况暂停。\\\\n302:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_MULTI_RUNTIME_SKILL_END -->\\\\n303:\\\\n304:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_1_SKILL_BEGIN -->\\\\n305:## Story OS V2.0.1 — Executable CODEX Production\\\\n306:\\\\n307:CODEX runtime 提供机器可执行入口 `story_os.py run <episode> --full-auto`，并提供基于当前 Codex ChatGPT 登录态的单图 backend `codex_subscription_image.py`。这两者只补执行能力，不建立第二状态机、不改变主规范、不伪造人工批准。\\\\n308:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_1_SKILL_END -->\\\\n309:\\\\n310:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_2_SKILL_BEGIN -->\\\\n311:## Story OS V2.0.2 Production Closure\\\\n312:\\\\n313:Full-auto pipeline: `worker → deterministic postflight → COMPLETE|PAUSED|BLOCKED`。图片链路必须 `raw → normalize → exact ledger canvas`。全自动批准使用 delegated provenance，不伪装 direct user review；最终 ZIP 必须通过 delegated delivery verify。\\\\n314:<!-- STORY_OS_V2_0_2_SKILL_END -->\\\\n315:\\\\n316:\\\\n317:## V2.0.3.3 Frame Semantic Enforcement\\\\n318:\\\\n319:- `actual_frame_semantic_review`：独立 Critic 审实际最终图片，而不是 prompt。\\\\n320:- `sha_bound_frame_reviews`：每帧 review 必须绑定当前 approved asset SHA。\\\\n321:- `release_evidence_closure`：Release 前再次执行 Production semantic preflight，交付包携带 frame review / audit。\\\\n322:- recovered/locked 资产没有当前 SHA 的 schema 2 review 时不得继承 PASS。\\\\n323:- 不新增第八状态。\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\r\\nepisodes/10_山难伪纪录片/01_鳌太线_热汤/media/review\\\\generation-20.jsonl:34:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.cache\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\native\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pwsh.exe\\\\\\\" -Command \\\\\\\"Get-Content -Raw -Encoding UTF8 'C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\skills\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.system\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\imagegen\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\SKILL.md'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\r\\nepisodes/10_山难伪纪录片/01_鳌太线_热汤/media/review\\\\generation-20.jsonl:35:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.cache\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\native\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pwsh.exe\\\\\\\" -Command \\\\\\\"Get-Content -Raw -Encoding UTF8 'C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\skills\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.system\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\imagegen\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\SKILL.md'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"---\\\\r\\\\nname: \\\\\\\"imagegen\\\\\\\"\\\\r\\\\ndescription: \\\\\\\"Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas.\\\\\\\"\\\\r\\\\n---\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n# Image Generation Skill\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nGenerates or edits images for the current project (for example website assets, game assets, UI mockups, product mockups, wireframes, logo design, photorealistic images, or infographics).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Top-level modes and rules\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThis skill has exactly two top-level modes:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- **Default built-in tool mode (preferred):** built-in `image_gen` tool for normal image generation, editing, and simple transparent-image requests. Does not require `OPENAI_API_KEY`.\\\\r\\\\n- **Fallback CLI mode:** `scripts/image_gen.py` CLI. Use when the user explicitly asks for the CLI/API/model path, or after the user explicitly confirms a true model-native transparency fallback with `gpt-image-1.5`. Requires `OPENAI_API_KEY`.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWithin CLI fallback, the CLI exposes three subcommands:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- `generate`\\\\r\\\\n- `edit`\\\\r\\\\n- `generate-batch`\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nRules:\\\\r\\\\n- Use the built-in `image_gen` tool by default for normal image generation and editing requests.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not switch to CLI fallback for ordinary quality, size, or file-path control.\\\\r\\\\n- If the user explicitly asks for a transparent image/background, stay on built-in `image_gen` first: prompt for a flat removable chroma-key background, then remove it locally with the installed helper at `$CODEX_HOME/skills/.system/imagegen/scripts/remove_chroma_key.py`.\\\\r\\\\n- Never silently switch from built-in `image_gen` or CLI `gpt-image-2` to CLI `gpt-image-1.5`. Treat this as a model/path downgrade and ask the user before doing it, unless the user has already explicitly requested `gpt-image-1.5`, `scripts/image_gen.py`, or CLI fallback.\\\\r\\\\n- If a transparent request appears too complex for clean chroma-key removal, asks for true/native transparency, or local removal fails validation, explain that true transparency requires CLI `gpt-image-1.5 --background transparent --output-format png` because `gpt-image-2` does not support `background=transparent`, then ask whether to proceed. Run the CLI fallback only after the user confirms.\\\\r\\\\n- The word `batch` by itself does not mean CLI fallback. If the user asks for many assets or says to batch-generate assets without explicitly asking for CLI/API/model controls, stay on the built-in path and issue one built-in call per requested asset or variant.\\\\r\\\\n- If the built-in tool fails or is unavailable, tell the user the CLI fallback exists and that it requires `OPENAI_API_KEY`. Proceed only if the user explicitly asks for that fallback.\\\\r\\\\n- If the user explicitly asks for CLI mode, use the bundled `scripts/image_gen.py` workflow. Do not create one-off SDK runners.\\\\r\\\\n- Never modify `scripts/image_gen.py`. If something is missing, ask the user before doing anything else.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nBuilt-in save-path policy:\\\\r\\\\n- In built-in tool mode, Codex saves generated images under `$CODEX_HOME/*` by default.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not describe or rely on OS temp as the default built-in destination.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not describe or rely on a destination-path argument (if any) on the built-in `image_gen` tool. If a specific location is needed, generate first and then move or copy the selected output from `$CODEX_HOME/generated_images/...`.\\\\r\\\\n- Save-path precedence in built-in mode:\\\\r\\\\n  1. If the user names a destination, move or copy the selected output there.\\\\r\\\\n  2. If the image is meant for the current project, move or copy the final selected image into the workspace before finishing.\\\\r\\\\n  3. If the image is only for preview or brainstorming, render it inline; the underlying file can remain at the default `$CODEX_HOME/*` path.\\\\r\\\\n- Never leave a project-referenced asset only at the default `$CODEX_HOME/*` path.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not overwrite an existing asset unless the user explicitly asked for replacement; otherwise create a sibling versioned filename such as `hero-v2.png` or `item-icon-edited.png`.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nShared prompt guidance for both modes lives in `references/prompting.md` and `references/sample-prompts.md`.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFallback-only docs/resources for CLI mode:\\\\r\\\\n- `references/cli.md`\\\\r\\\\n- `references/image-api.md`\\\\r\\\\n- `references/codex-network.md`\\\\r\\\\n- `scripts/image_gen.py`\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLocal post-processing helper:\\\\r\\\\n- `$CODEX_HOME/skills/.system/imagegen/scripts/remove_chroma_key.py`: removes a flat chroma-key background from a generated image and writes a PNG/WebP with alpha. Prefer auto-key sampling, soft matte, and despill for antialiased edges.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## When to use\\\\r\\\\n- Generate a new image (concept art, product shot, cover, website hero)\\\\r\\\\n- Generate a new image using one or more reference images for style, composition, or mood\\\\r\\\\n- Edit an existing image (inpainting, lighting or weather transformations, background replacement, object removal, compositing, transparent background)\\\\r\\\\n- Produce many assets or variants for one task\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## When not to use\\\\r\\\\n- Extending or matching an existing SVG/vector icon set, logo system, or illustration library inside the repo\\\\r\\\\n- Creating simple shapes, diagrams, wireframes, or icons that are better produced directly in SVG, HTML/CSS, or canvas\\\\r\\\\n- Making a small project-local asset edit when the source file already exists in an editable native format\\\\r\\\\n- Any task where the user clearly wants deterministic code-native output instead of a generated bitmap\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Decision tree\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThink about two separate questions:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n1. **Intent:** is this a new image or an edit of an existing image?\\\\r\\\\n2. **Execution strategy:** is this one asset or many assets/variants?\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIntent:\\\\r\\\\n- If the user wants to modify an existing image while preserving parts of it, treat the request as **edit**.\\\\r\\\\n- If the user provides images only as references for style, composition, mood, or subject guidance, treat the request as **generate**.\\\\r\\\\n- If the user provides no images, treat the request as **generate**.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nBuilt-in edit semantics:\\\\r\\\\n- Built-in edit mode is for images already visible in the conversation context, such as attached images or images generated earlier in the thread.\\\\r\\\\n- If the user wants to edit a local image file with the built-in tool, first load it with built-in `view_image` tool so the image is visible in the conversation context, then proceed with the built-in edit flow.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not promise arbitrary filesystem-path editing through the built-in tool.\\\\r\\\\n- If a local file still needs direct file-path control, masks, or other explicit CLI-only parameters, use the explicit CLI fallback only when the user asks for it.\\\\r\\\\n- For edits, preserve invariants aggressively and save non-destructively by default.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nExecution strategy:\\\\r\\\\n- In the built-in default path, produce many assets or variants by issuing one `image_gen` call per requested asset or variant.\\\\r\\\\n- In the CLI fallback path, use the CLI `generate-batch` subcommand only when the user explicitly chose CLI mode and needs many prompts/assets.\\\\r\\\\n- For many distinct assets, do not use `n` as a substitute for separate prompts. `n` is for variants of one prompt; distinct assets need distinct built-in calls or distinct CLI `generate-batch` jobs.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAssume the user wants a new image unless they clearly ask to change an existing one.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Workflow\\\\r\\\\n1. Decide the top-level mode: built-in by default, including simple transparent-output requests; fallback CLI only if explicitly requested or after the user explicitly confirms a transparent-output fallback.\\\\r\\\\n2. Decide the intent: `generate` or `edit`.\\\\r\\\\n3. Decide whether the output is preview-only or meant to be consumed by the current project.\\\\r\\\\n4. Decide the execution strategy: single asset vs repeated built-in calls vs CLI `generate-batch`.\\\\r\\\\n5. Collect inputs up front: prompt(s), exact text (verbatim), constraints/avoid list, and any input images.\\\\r\\\\n6. For every input image, label its role explicitly:\\\\r\\\\n   - reference image\\\\r\\\\n   - edit target\\\\r\\\\n   - supporting insert/style/compositing input\\\\r\\\\n7. If the edit target is only on the local filesystem and you are staying on the built-in path, inspect it with `view_image` first so the image is available in conversation context.\\\\r\\\\n8. If the user asked for a photo, illustration, sprite, product image, banner, or other explicitly raster-style asset, use `image_gen` rather than substituting SVG/HTML/CSS placeholders. If the request is for an icon, logo, or UI graphic that should match existing repo-native SVG/vector/code assets, prefer editing those directly instead.\\\\r\\\\n9. Augment the prompt based on specificity:\\\\r\\\\n   - If the user's prompt is already specific and detailed, normalize it into a clear spec without adding creative requirements.\\\\r\\\\n   - If the user's prompt is generic, add tasteful augmentation only when it materially improves output quality.\\\\r\\\\n10. Use the built-in `image_gen` tool by default.\\\\r\\\\n11. For transparent-output requests, follow the transparent image guidance below: generate with built-in `image_gen` on a flat chroma-key background, copy the selected output into the workspace or `tmp/imagegen/`, run the installed `$CODEX_HOME/skills/.system/imagegen/scripts/remove_chroma_key.py` helper, and validate the alpha result before using it. If this path looks unsuitable or fails, ask before switching to CLI `gpt-image-1.5`.\\\\r\\\\n12. Inspect outputs and validate: subject, style, composition, text accuracy, and invariants/avoid items.\\\\r\\\\n13. Iterate with a single targeted change, then re-check.\\\\r\\\\n14. For preview-only work, render the image inline; the underlying file may remain at the default `$CODEX_HOME/generated_images/...` path.\\\\r\\\\n15. For project-bound work, move or copy the selected artifact into the workspace and update any consuming code or references. Never leave a project-referenced asset only at the default `$CODEX_HOME/generated_images/...` path.\\\\r\\\\n16. For batches or multi-asset requests, persist every requested deliverable final in the workspace unless the user explicitly asked to keep outputs preview-only. Discarded variants do not need to be kept unless requested.\\\\r\\\\n17. If the user explicitly chooses or confirms the CLI fallback, then use the fallback-only docs for model, quality, size, `input_fidelity`, masks, output format, output paths, and network setup.\\\\r\\\\n18. Always report the final saved path(s) for any workspace-bound asset(s), plus the final prompt or prompt set and whether the built-in tool or fallback CLI mode was used.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Transparent image requests\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTransparent-image requests still use built-in `image_gen` first. Because the built-in tool does not expose a true transparent-background control, create a removable chroma-key source image and then convert the key color to alpha locally.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nDefault sequence:\\\\r\\\\n1. Use built-in `image_gen` to generate the requested subject on a perfectly flat solid chroma-key background.\\\\r\\\\n2. Choose a key color that is unlikely to appear in the subject: default `#00ff00`, use `#ff00ff` for green subjects, and avoid `#0000ff` for blue subjects.\\\\r\\\\n3. After generation, move or copy the selected source image from `$CODEX_HOME/generated_images/...` into the workspace or `tmp/imagegen/`.\\\\r\\\\n4. Run the installed helper path, not a project-relative script path:\\\\r\\\\n   ```bash\\\\r\\\\n   python \\\\\\\"${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/skills/.system/imagegen/scripts/remove_chroma_key.py\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\n     --input <source> \\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\n     --out <final.png> \\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\n     --auto-key border \\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\n     --soft-matte \\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\n     --transparent-threshold 12 \\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\n     --opaque-threshold 220 \\\\\\\\\\\\r\\\\n     --despill\\\\r\\\\n   ```\\\\r\\\\n5. Validate that the output has an alpha channel, transparent corners, plausible subject coverage, and no obvious key-color fringe. If a thin fringe remains, retry once with `--edge-contract 1`; use `--edge-feather 0.25` only when the edge is visibly stair-stepped and the subject is not shiny or reflective.\\\\r\\\\n6. Save the final alpha PNG/WebP in the project if the asset is project-bound. Never leave a project-referenced transparent asset only under `$CODEX_HOME/*`.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPrompt transparent requests like this:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n```text\\\\r\\\\nCreate the requested subject on a perfectly flat solid #00ff00 chroma-key background for background removal.\\\\r\\\\nThe background must be one uniform color with no shadows, gradients, texture, reflections, floor plane, or lighting variation.\\\\r\\\\nKeep the subject fully separated from the background with crisp edges and generous padding.\\\\r\\\\nDo not use #00ff00 anywhere in the subject.\\\\r\\\\nNo cast shadow, no contact shadow, no reflection, no watermark, and no text unless explicitly requested.\\\\r\\\\n```\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nDo not automatically use CLI `gpt-image-1.5 --background transparent --output-format png` instead of chroma keying. Ask the user first when the user asks for true/native transparency, when local removal fails validation, or when the requested image is complex: hair, fur, feathers, smoke, glass, liquids, translucent materials, reflective objects, soft shadows, realistic product grounding, or subject colors that conflict with all practical key colors.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nUse a concise confirmation like:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n```text\\\\r\\\\nThis likely needs true native transparency. The default built-in path uses a chroma-key background plus local removal, but true transparency requires the CLI fallback with gpt-image-1.5 because gpt-image-2 does not support background=transparent. It also requires OPENAI_API_KEY. Should I proceed with that CLI fallback?\\\\r\\\\n```\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Prompt augmentation\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nReformat user prompts into a structured, production-oriented spec. Make the user's goal clearer and more actionable, but do not blindly add detail.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTreat this as prompt-shaping guidance, not a closed schema. Use only the lines that help, and add a short extra labeled line when it materially improves clarity.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### Specificity policy\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nUse the user's prompt specificity to decide how much augmentation is appropriate:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- If the prompt is already specific and detailed, preserve that specificity and only normalize/structure it.\\\\r\\\\n- If the prompt is generic, you may add tasteful augmentation when it will materially improve the result.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAllowed augmentations:\\\\r\\\\n- composition or framing hints\\\\r\\\\n- polish level or intended-use hints\\\\r\\\\n- practical layout guidance\\\\r\\\\n- reasonable scene concreteness that supports the stated request\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNot allowed augmentations:\\\\r\\\\n- extra characters or objects that are not implied by the request\\\\r\\\\n- brand names, slogans, palettes, or narrative beats that are not implied\\\\r\\\\n- arbitrary side-specific placement unless the surrounding layout supports it\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Use-case taxonomy (exact slugs)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nClassify each request into one of these buckets and keep the slug consistent across prompts and references.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nGenerate:\\\\r\\\\n- photorealistic-natural — candid/editorial lifestyle scenes with real texture and natural lighting.\\\\r\\\\n- product-mockup — product/packaging shots, catalog imagery, merch concepts.\\\\r\\\\n- ui-mockup — app/web interface mockups and wireframes; specify the desired fidelity.\\\\r\\\\n- infographic-diagram — diagrams/infographics with structured layout and text.\\\\r\\\\n- scientific-educational — classroom explainers, scientific diagrams, and learning visuals with required labels and accuracy constraints.\\\\r\\\\n- ads-marketing — campaign concepts and ad creatives with audience, brand position, scene, and exact tagline/copy.\\\\r\\\\n- productivity-visual — slide, chart, workflow, and data-heavy business visuals.\\\\r\\\\n- logo-brand — logo/mark exploration, vector-friendly.\\\\r\\\\n- illustration-story — comics, children’s book art, narrative scenes.\\\\r\\\\n- stylized-concept — style-driven concept art, 3D/stylized renders.\\\\r\\\\n- historical-scene — period-accurate/world-knowledge scenes.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nEdit:\\\\r\\\\n- text-localization — translate/replace in-image text, preserve layout.\\\\r\\\\n- identity-preserve — try-on, person-in-scene; lock face/body/pose.\\\\r\\\\n- precise-object-edit — remove/replace a specific element (including interior swaps).\\\\r\\\\n- lighting-weather — time-of-day/season/atmosphere changes only.\\\\r\\\\n- background-extraction — transparent background / clean cutout. Use built-in `image_gen` with chroma-key removal first for simple opaque subjects; ask before using CLI true transparency for complex subjects.\\\\r\\\\n- style-transfer — apply reference style while changing subject/scene.\\\\r\\\\n- compositing — multi-image insert/merge with matched lighting/perspective.\\\\r\\\\n- sketch-to-render — drawing/line art to photoreal render.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Shared prompt schema\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nUse the following labeled spec as shared prompt scaffolding for both top-level modes:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n```text\\\\r\\\\nUse case: <taxonomy slug>\\\\r\\\\nAsset type: <where the asset will be used>\\\\r\\\\nPrimary request: <user's main prompt>\\\\r\\\\nInput images: <Image 1: role; Image 2: role> (optional)\\\\r\\\\nScene/backdrop: <environment>\\\\r\\\\nSubject: <main subject>\\\\r\\\\nStyle/medium: <photo/illustration/3D/etc>\\\\r\\\\nComposition/framing: <wide/close/top-down; placement>\\\\r\\\\nLighting/mood: <lighting + mood>\\\\r\\\\nColor palette: <palette notes>\\\\r\\\\nMaterials/textures: <surface details>\\\\r\\\\nText (verbatim): \\\\\\\"<exact text>\\\\\\\"\\\\r\\\\nConstraints: <must keep/must avoid>\\\\r\\\\nAvoid: <negative constraints>\\\\r\\\\n```\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNotes:\\\\r\\\\n- `Asset type` and `Input images` are prompt scaffolding, not dedicated CLI flags.\\\\r\\\\n- `Scene/backdrop` refers to the visual setting. It is not the same as the fallback CLI `background` parameter, which controls output transparency behavior.\\\\r\\\\n- Fallback-only execution notes such as `Quality:`, `Input fidelity:`, masks, output format, and output paths belong in the CLI path only. Do not treat them as built-in `image_gen` tool arguments.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAugmentation rules:\\\\r\\\\n- Keep it short.\\\\r\\\\n- Add only the details needed to improve the prompt materially.\\\\r\\\\n- For edits, explicitly list invariants (`change only X; keep Y unchanged`).\\\\r\\\\n- If any critical detail is missing and blocks success, ask a question; otherwise proceed.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Examples\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### Generation example (hero image)\\\\r\\\\n```text\\\\r\\\\nUse case: product-mockup\\\\r\\\\nAsset type: landing page hero\\\\r\\\\nPrimary request: a minimal hero image of a ceramic coffee mug\\\\r\\\\nStyle/medium: clean product photography\\\\r\\\\nComposition/framing: wide composition with usable negative space for page copy if needed\\\\r\\\\nLighting/mood: soft studio lighting\\\\r\\\\nConstraints: no logos, no text, no watermark\\\\r\\\\n```\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### Edit example (invariants)\\\\r\\\\n```text\\\\r\\\\nUse case: precise-object-edit\\\\r\\\\nAsset type: product photo background replacement\\\\r\\\\nPrimary request: replace only the background with a warm sunset gradient\\\\r\\\\nConstraints: change only the background; keep the product and its edges unchanged; no text; no watermark\\\\r\\\\n```\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Prompting best practices\\\\r\\\\n- Structure prompt as scene/backdrop -> subject -> details -> constraints.\\\\r\\\\n- Include intended use (ad, UI mock, infographic) to set the mode and polish level.\\\\r\\\\n- Use camera/composition language for photorealism.\\\\r\\\\n- Only use SVG/vector stand-ins when the user explicitly asked for vector output or a non-image placeholder.\\\\r\\\\n- Quote exact text and specify typography + placement.\\\\r\\\\n- For tricky words, spell them letter-by-letter and require verbatim rendering.\\\\r\\\\n- For multi-image inputs, reference images by index and describe how they should be used.\\\\r\\\\n- For edits, repeat invariants every iteration to reduce drift.\\\\r\\\\n- Iterate with single-change follow-ups.\\\\r\\\\n- If the prompt is generic, add only the extra detail that will materially help.\\\\r\\\\n- If the prompt is already detailed, normalize it instead of expanding it.\\\\r\\\\n- For CLI fallback only, see `references/cli.md` and `references/image-api.md` for model, `quality`, `input_fidelity`, masks, output format, and output-path guidance.\\\\r\\\\n- For transparent images, use the built-in-first chroma-key workflow unless the request is complex enough to need true CLI transparency; ask before switching to CLI `gpt-image-1.5`.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMore principles shared by both modes: `references/prompting.md`.\\\\r\\\\nCopy/paste specs shared by both modes: `references/sample-prompts.md`.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Guidance by asset type\\\\r\\\\nAsset-type templates (website assets, game assets, wireframes, logo) are consolidated in `references/sample-prompts.md`.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## gpt-image-2 guidance for CLI fallback\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe fallback CLI defaults to `gpt-image-2`.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Use `gpt-image-2` for new CLI/API workflows unless the request needs true model-native transparent output.\\\\r\\\\n- If a transparent request may need CLI fallback, ask before using `gpt-image-1.5` unless the user already explicitly requested `gpt-image-1.5`, `scripts/image_gen.py`, or CLI fallback. Explain that the built-in chroma-key path is the default, but true transparency requires `gpt-image-1.5` because `gpt-image-2` does not support `background=transparent`.\\\\r\\\\n- `gpt-image-2` always uses high fidelity for image inputs; do not set `input_fidelity` with this model.\\\\r\\\\n- `gpt-image-2` supports `quality` values `low`, `medium`, `high`, and `auto`.\\\\r\\\\n- Use `quality low` for fast drafts, thumbnails, and quick iterations. Use `medium`, `high`, or `auto` for final assets, dense text, diagrams, identity-sensitive edits, or high-resolution outputs.\\\\r\\\\n- Square images are typically fastest to generate. Use `1024x1024` for fast square drafts.\\\\r\\\\n- If the user asks for 4K-style output, use `3840x2160` for landscape or `2160x3840` for portrait.\\\\r\\\\n- `gpt-image-2` size may be `auto` or `WIDTHxHEIGHT` if all constraints hold: max edge `<= 3840px`, both edges multiples of `16px`, long-to-short ratio `<= 3:1`, total pixels between `655,360` and `8,294,400`.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPopular `gpt-image-2` sizes:\\\\r\\\\n- `1024x1024` square\\\\r\\\\n- `1536x1024` landscape\\\\r\\\\n- `1024x1536` portrait\\\\r\\\\n- `2048x2048` 2K square\\\\r\\\\n- `2048x1152` 2K landscape\\\\r\\\\n- `3840x2160` 4K landscape\\\\r\\\\n- `2160x3840` 4K portrait\\\\r\\\\n- `auto`\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Fallback CLI mode only\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### Temp and output conventions\\\\r\\\\nThese conventions apply only to the CLI fallback. They do not describe built-in `image_gen` output behavior.\\\\r\\\\n- Use `tmp/imagegen/` for intermediate files (for example JSONL batches); delete them when done.\\\\r\\\\n- Write final artifacts under `output/imagegen/`.\\\\r\\\\n- Use `--out` or `--out-dir` to control output paths; keep filenames stable and descriptive.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### Dependencies\\\\r\\\\nPrefer `uv` for dependency management in this repo.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nRequired Python package:\\\\r\\\\n```bash\\\\r\\\\nuv pip install openai\\\\r\\\\n```\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nRequired for local chroma-key removal and optional downscaling:\\\\r\\\\n```bash\\\\r\\\\nuv pip install pillow\\\\r\\\\n```\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPortability note:\\\\r\\\\n- If you are using the installed skill outside this repo, install dependencies into that environment with its package manager.\\\\r\\\\n- In uv-managed environments, `uv pip install ...` remains the preferred path.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### Environment\\\\r\\\\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY` must be set for live API calls.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not ask the user for `OPENAI_API_KEY` when using the built-in `image_gen` tool.\\\\r\\\\n- Never ask the user to paste the full key in chat. Ask them to set it locally and confirm when ready.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIf the key is missing, give the user these steps:\\\\r\\\\n1. Create an API key in the OpenAI platform UI: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys\\\\r\\\\n2. Set `OPENAI_API_KEY` as an environment variable in their system.\\\\r\\\\n3. Offer to guide them through setting the environment variable for their OS/shell if needed.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIf installation is not possible in this environment, tell the user which dependency is missing and how to install it into their active environment.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### Script-mode notes\\\\r\\\\n- CLI commands + examples: `references/cli.md`\\\\r\\\\n- API parameter quick reference: `references/image-api.md`\\\\r\\\\n- Network approvals / sandbox settings for CLI mode: `references/codex-network.md`\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Reference map\\\\r\\\\n- `references/prompting.md`: shared prompting principles for both modes.\\\\r\\\\n- `references/sample-prompts.md`: shared copy/paste prompt recipes for both modes.\\\\r\\\\n- `references/cli.md`: fallback-only CLI usage via `scripts/image_gen.py`.\\\\r\\\\n- `references/image-api.md`: fallback-only API/CLI parameter reference.\\\\r\\\\n- `references/codex-network.md`: fallback-only network/sandbox troubleshooting for CLI mode.\\\\r\\\\n- `scripts/image_gen.py`: fallback-only CLI implementation. Do not load or use it unless the user explicitly chooses CLI mode or explicitly confirms a transparent request's true CLI transparency fallback.\\\\r\\\\n- `$CODEX_HOME/skills/.system/imagegen/scripts/remove_chroma_key.py`: local post-processing helper for built-in transparent-image requests.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\r\\nepisodes/10_山难伪纪录片/01_鳌太线_热汤/media/review\\\\generation-20.jsonl:54:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.cache\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\native\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pwsh.exe\\\\\\\" -Command '$root = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE '\\\\\\\"'.codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\generated_images'; Get-ChildItem -Path \\\\\\\"'$root -Recurse -File -ErrorAction Stop | Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 8 FullName,Length,LastWriteTime'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\r\\nepisodes/10_山难伪纪录片/01_鳌太线_热汤/media/review\\\\generation-20.jsonl:55:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.cache\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\native\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pwsh.exe\\\\\\\" -Command '$root = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE '\\\\\\\"'.codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\generated_images'; Get-ChildItem -Path \\\\\\\"'$root -Recurse -File -ErrorAction Stop | Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 8 FullName,Length,LastWriteTime'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\\r\\\\nFullName\\\\r\\\\n--------                                                                       \\\\r\\\\nC:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\.codex\\\\\\\\generated_images\\\\\\\\01a04e10-e4ac-7fa3-a631-eec648569854\\\\\\\\ig…\\\\r\\\\nC:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\79873\\\\\\\\.codex\\\\\\\\generated_images\\\\\\\\01a04e04-b49b-7990-abf1-46f